{
  "comment": "Where a request came from, as every agent decides it: `origin` is the network class a txn or page record carries, `address` the hop that decided it — hashed into the anonymous visitor, never sent. Behind Cloudflare (CF-Connecting-IP, or a bare CF-Ray) it is a tunnel. Otherwise the chain is X-Forwarded-For then the socket's peer, walked from the nearest hop outwards: the first address that is not private decides (100.64.0.0/10 says vpn). A chain private all the way out is the LAN, decided by its outermost hop. Something that is not an address decides nothing.",
  "cases": [
    { "remote": "127.0.0.1", "origin": "lan", "address": "127.0.0.1" },
    { "remote": "::ffff:192.168.1.20", "origin": "lan", "address": "::ffff:192.168.1.20" },
    { "remote": "::1", "origin": "lan", "address": "::1" },
    { "remote": "127.0.0.1", "forwarded": "100.88.12.34", "origin": "vpn", "address": "100.88.12.34" },
    { "remote": "172.18.0.5", "forwarded": "100.88.7.21", "origin": "vpn", "address": "100.88.7.21" },
    { "remote": "127.0.0.1", "forwarded": "192.168.1.5, 8.8.8.8", "origin": "public", "address": "8.8.8.8" },
    { "remote": "10.0.0.2", "forwarded": "192.168.1.5, 203.0.113.9", "origin": "public", "address": "203.0.113.9" },
    { "remote": "172.18.0.5", "forwarded": "198.51.100.77, 203.0.113.9", "origin": "public", "address": "203.0.113.9" },
    { "remote": "172.18.0.5", "forwarded": "192.168.1.5, 10.0.0.3", "origin": "lan", "address": "192.168.1.5" },
    { "remote": "2606:4700::1111", "origin": "public", "address": "2606:4700::1111" },
    { "remote": "172.18.0.5", "forwarded": "fd7a:115c:a1e0::1", "origin": "lan", "address": "fd7a:115c:a1e0::1" },
    { "remote": "10.0.0.2", "forwarded": "8.8.8.8", "cf_connecting_ip": "203.0.113.7", "origin": "tunnel", "address": "203.0.113.7" },
    { "remote": "10.0.0.2", "forwarded": "198.51.100.4, 172.18.0.1", "cf_ray": "8c1f2a90b1d2e3f4-LHR", "origin": "tunnel", "address": "198.51.100.4" },
    { "remote": "junk", "origin": "lan", "address": "junk" },
    { "remote": "172.18.0.5", "forwarded": "not-an-address, 192.168.1.5", "origin": "lan", "address": "not-an-address" },
    { "origin": null, "address": null }
  ],
  "propagate_comment": "Where an agent sends `traceparent` on an outbound request: to a host that is ours, never the public internet. A host that is an address (bracketed or not) is ours when the origin rule above does not call it public — private, link-local, a ULA, 100.64.0.0/10, or a VPN range the app configured. A host that is not an address is ours when it is bare (no dot: a container network's names), or is or ends in a suffix: the internal ones every client knows (lan, local, internal) plus those the app configured, compared without case. `propagate_to` is the configuration these cases are run with.",
  "propagate_to": ["example.net"],
